Package: mysterycall
Title: Mystery Caller Study Tools for Healthcare Access Research
Version: 1.6.0
Authors@R:
    person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2044-1693"))
Description: Tools for design, analysis, and reporting of mystery-caller (secret-shopper)
    studies that measure healthcare access disparities. Provides generalized linear mixed
    models (Poisson and negative-binomial GLMMs) for wait-time outcomes, incidence rate
    ratios with confidence intervals, IRR-to-absolute-days conversion, model selection
    and overdispersion diagnostics, intraclass correlation coefficients, Monte Carlo power
    curves, CONSORT/STROBE flow diagrams, inter-caller reliability, missing-data MAR/MNAR
    tests, and one-call manuscript generators for results, materials-and-methods, and
    STROBE-checklist sections. Also includes utilities for National Provider Identifier
    (NPI) record lookup and enrichment pipeline, provider demographics, Medicaid expansion
    status dataset, calendar-vs-business-day sensitivity analysis, broom-compatible tidy()
    methods, REDCap data dictionary parser, and publication-ready table and map output.
